What:		/proc/game_opt/game_pid
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read/write ColorOS 14 GameOpt process selector.  Writing a positive
		process leader PID starts bounded CFS/RT runtime accounting for that
		process.  Writing zero or a negative value stops accounting and
		releases the selection.  Reading returns the selected PID or -1.

What:		/proc/game_opt/heavy_task_info
Date:		September 2026
Contact:	KAI-Miru kernel maintainers
Description:
		Read-only, reset-on-read task runtime report for the process selected
		through game_pid.  At most ten active threads are returned, sorted by
		frequency- and capacity-scaled utilization, using this grammar:

		<tid>;<comm>;<util>

		util is clamped to the donor-compatible range 0..1024.  Runtime
		accounting is disabled until userspace selects a valid process and
		the scheduler hooks use a non-blocking lock with a 256-thread cap.
Users:		vendor.oplus.hardware.gameopt-service
